		holds. Since $\mathrm{spec}(M) \subset \R$ if $M$ is Hermitian, this immediately implies the first bound. The well-known resolvent identity $G(\ii \eta,  M) - G(\ii \eta, M^\prime) = G(\ii \eta,  M) (M-M^{\prime}) G(\ii \eta, M^\prime)$ and the first bound directly yield the second and third","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:47c949780f2914da33d74b535f3bbbbbd70a7f0eb9036427b6d876e3e177ddfb","revision_digest":"sha256:e956a2726614d6c61c1d59feabbdfac682e5707385b909c0a254039c9e96bd50","source_id":"arxiv:2606.24887","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

