[Lemma 47 of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] Let $f\in \H^{\otimes n}$ and $g\in \H^{\otimes m}$. For any $p\leqs n\wedge m$, 
all $x\in\Lambda^{n-p}$ and all $y\in\Lambda^{m-p}$, one has
\begin{equation}
 (f \star_p g)(x,y) 
 = \sum_{\substack{\Sigma\in\frakS(p,n)\\ \bar\Sigma\in\frakS(p,m)}}
 \sum_{\sigma\in\frakS(p)}
 \int_{\Lambda^p} f\bigpar{\Sigma(z,x)}g\bigpar{\bar\Sigma(z,\sigma(x))} \6z\;.
\end{equation}

