[Theorem thm:PP conv general of arXiv:2607.01946, 'Second-order fluctuations for a phase transition in random partitions'] For $(p_n)_{n\in{\mathbb N}}$ under the assumption (equation eq:p_n general of the paper), we have
\begin{equation}
\xi'_n\Rightarrow {\rm PPP}\pp{{\mathbb R}\times{\mathbb R}\times[0,\infty),\mu_\alpha({\rm d} x){\rm d} y e^{-z}{\rm d} z}, \end{equation}
as $n\to\infty$ in $\mathcal{M}_p({\mathbb R}\times{\mathbb R}\times[0,\infty))$. Moreover, 
\[
\pp{\mathcal{Z}_n'(t)}_{t\in{\mathbb R}}\Rightarrow \pp{\mathcal{Z}(t)}_{t\in{\mathbb R}}
\]
in $D({\mathbb R},\mathcal{M}_{p,f}({\mathbb R}))$,  and
 \[
 \pp{C_{j_n}(\floor{s_n(t)})}_{t\in{\mathbb R}} \Rightarrow ({\mathcal C}_{\alpha,r}(t))_{t\in{\mathbb R}}
 \]
 in $D({\mathbb R})$ as $n\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition pro:bound_V_Holder of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $F \in \mathcal{C}^2$. There exists a constants $C=C(\|F\|_{\mathcal{C}^2}, \|\sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^2}, H_-)$ and $q=q(H_-)$ such that for all $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$, $s\in [0,1]$ and ${\color{blue}M}= (M, M') \in \mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])$, if $V$ is a solution of (equation eq:general_equation_Jacobian of the paper), then 
       \begin{equs}
\|{\color{blue}V}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])} \leq C (1+[{\color{blue}B}]_{\mathcal{R}^{H_-}})^q ( \|V\|_{\mathcal{C}^0([s,1])}+\|{\color{blue}M}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s,1])}).
   \end{equs}

