[Definition def:def4.1 of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] Given a finite subset $\Lambda \subseteq \ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2$, a collection of conductances $\left( J_{xy} \right)_{xy \in E(\Lambda)} \in [0, \infty)^{E(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}^2)}$, we define the integer-valued Gaussian free field on the set $\Lambda$ with conductances $J = (J_{xy})$ to be the probability distribution on the set $\Omega_\Lambda^\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ given by the identity
(recall the definition of the set $\Omega_\Lambda^\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}$ given above in~(equation e.ZGFF of the paper))

\begin{equation*} 
    \mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}} (\left\{ \varphi \right\}) := \frac{1}{Z_{\Lambda,J}} \exp \left( - \sum_{x \sim y}  \frac{\left( \varphi(x) - \varphi(y) \right)^2}{2J_{xy}} \right).
\end{equation*}
We denote by $\mathrm{Var}_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}}$ the variance with respect to the measure $\mu_{\Lambda , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}}$ and write $\mathrm{Var}_{L , J}^{\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}-\mathrm{GFF}}$ when $\Lambda = \Lambda_L$.

[Lemma lem:JordanLowerBoundUpper of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For the Jordan ordering $\widehat{\sigma}_J$, there exist positive constants $C$ and $c$ such that for any $n\geq 1$, any vertex $v\in [n]$ and any $S\geq 1$, 

    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}\left(\widehat{\sigma}_J(v)\leq \frac{v}{S}\right) \leq C \left( e^{- c v/S} +  e^{-S/64} \right).
    \end{equation}

