[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Assume that a controlled sequence $(\bar{X}^{\eta, xy}, \nu^\eta)$ converges to $(\bar{X}^{xy}, \nu)$.
    Then this limit satisfies, almost surely, the following integral equation on $[0,1)$
    \begin{equation}
        \bar{X}^{xy}_t = x + \int_0^{t} (b(s, \bar{X}^{xy}_s) + g^y(s, \bar{X}^{xy}_s) + \sigma(s, \bar{X}^{xy}_s) \nu_s) ds.
    \end{equation}

