body:
[Lemma reference-even-estimate of arXiv:2609.00425, 'Individual and Uniform Eventual Positivity of Self-Adjoint Semigroups'] There exists $C > 0$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \dual{\mathrm{e}^{nA_0}|_{H_{\mathrm{even}}} p_n, p_n} \leq \mathrm{e}^{-n^2} + C \mathrm{e}^{-3n^2}
    \end{align*}
    for all sufficiently large $n \in \mathbb{N}$.

