body:
[Prop 35 of arXiv:2609.01389, 'K-stability and birational rigidity of Fano 3-fold weighted complete intersections'] The following assertions hold.
\begin{enumerate}
\item If exactly one of $\alpha, \beta$ is zero and $\gamma \ne 0$, then there are infinitely many irreducible and reduced curves that intersect $B$ nonpositively.
\item Otherwise, the support of the $1$-cycle $\tilde{S}|_{\tilde{T}}$ consists of curves whose intersection matrix is negative-definite.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, $\msp$ is not a maximal center.

