[Lem func-WU of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Assume (fass1 of the paper), fix $\gamma = \gamma_b/2$ and define
    \begin{equation}
        \Psi(\phi) \coloneqq \ln\Big({1 + \sum_{i=1}^n c_ix_i}\Big) + A_2\int_{-r}^0\int_s^0 e^{\gamma (u-s)} h(\phi(u))dud\mu(s) \,,
    \end{equation}
    where $x_i = \phi_i(0)$ and $h, \mu$ are as in (fass1 of the paper). 
Then there are $p > 0, K > 0$ so that $W \coloneqq e^{p\Psi}$ and $U \coloneqq e^{2p\Psi}$ satisfy: \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item  $\mathcal{L} W \leq K - W'$,
        \item  $\mathcal{L} U \leq K - U'$,
        \item  $J + \Gamma W \lesssim U'$, where $J$ is as in (fass1 of the paper),
    \end{enumerate}
    where
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        W'(\phi) &\coloneqq pW(\phi)\Big(\gamma_0 + Ah(x) + \frac{A_2\gamma}{2}\int_{-r}^0\int_s^0 e^{\gamma (u-s)} h(\phi(s))dud\mu(s) + \frac{\gamma_b}{2}J(\phi)\Big) \\
        U'(\phi) &\coloneqq 2pU(\phi)\Big(\gamma_0 + Ah(x) + \frac{A_2\gamma}{2}\int_{-r}^0\int_s^0 e^{\gamma (u-s)} h(\phi(s))dud\mu(s) + \frac{\gamma_b}{2}J(\phi)\Big)
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
and $A = A_1 - A_2 \int e^{-\gamma s}d\mu(s) > 0$ (see (fass1 of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 4 of arXiv:2609.02173, 'Bounding Selmer Groups of Superelliptic Jacobians via Class Groups'] The maps \(\delta_F\) and
		$
		i\circ e\circ\kappa_{F,\Pi}
		$
		coincide as maps from \(J(F)/\Pi J(F)\) to
		\(L^\times/L^{\times p}\). More precisely, the diagram
		\[
		\xymatrix{
			J(F)/\Pi J(F)
			\ar[r]^{\kappa_{F,\Pi}}
			\ar[dr]_{\delta_F}
			&
			H^1(F,J[\Pi])
			\ar[d]^{\,i\circ e}
			\\
			&
			L^\times/L^{\times p}
		}
		\]
		is commutative.

