[Lemma dennear of arXiv:2512.19897, 'On the convoy of the ASEP speed process'] Let $w\left(x\right)$ be the density function of the reference measure of $H_n\left(x|q\right)$, supported on $\left[-1,1\right]$. For fixed $q \in [0,1)$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{\epsilon \to 0} \sqrt{\epsilon}w\left( 1 - \epsilon\right) = \frac{\sqrt{2} \left(q;q\right)_{\infty}}{\pi}. 
    \end{equation}
    In addition, $\sqrt{1-x}w\left( x\right)$ has a uniform upper bound for $x \in [0,1]$.

