[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.23305, 'On extremes of a random walk with positive drift\\ over an intermediate regularly varying '] Assume that $a:=\E\xi>0$.
Let the distribution of $\tau$ be intermediate regularly varying at infinity and such that
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{|\xi|>x\} &=& o\biggl(\frac{\P\{\tau>x\}}{\E(\tau\wedge x)}\biggr)\quad\mbox{as }x\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray}
If $\tau$ does not depend on the future, then
\begin{eqnarray}
\P\{M_\tau>x\}\ \sim\ \P\{S_\tau>x\} &\sim& \P\{\tau>x/a\}\quad\mbox{as  } x\to\infty.
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 6 (Application to heavy tails -- random thresholds) of arXiv:2506.20789, 'Central limit theory for Peaks-over-Threshold partial sums of long memory linear time seri'] Let the Assumptions of Corollary~\ref{cor:heavy_det} hold. Then, with $k=\lfloor n \PP[X_0>u_n]  \rfloor$, it holds that, as $n\to\infty$,
\begin{align*}
  &
    n^{1-(d+1/(\nu \land 2))
    }
    q_{X_0}
    \left(
    1
    -
    \frac{k}{n}
    \right)
    \\&
    \cdot
    \
      \left(
      \frac
      {
      \sum_{i=1}^{k}
        \log(
        X_{n-i+1:n}
        /
        X_{n-k:n}
        )
      }
      {n \PP[X_0>u_n]}
      \ - \
      \EE[\log(X_0/u_n) \mid X_0>u_n]
      \right)
      \ \stackrel{\mathrm{d}}{\longrightarrow}\
      \frac{1}{\nu+1} Z_{\nu\land 2}.
  \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop local-CLT-DKS of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exist absolute constants $C,\beta_0>0$ such that for all $N\geq 1, -N\leq k \leq N$ and $\beta>\beta_0$, if $NM_{N,H}=k$ then
\begin{equation}
\frac{C^{-1}}{\sqrt{1+ND_H}}\leq P_{N,H}(h(S) = k) \leq \frac{C}{\sqrt{1+ND_H}} 
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
\frac{C^{-1}}{\sqrt{1+ND_H}}e^{N(F(H)-\beta H k)}\leq P_{N}(h(S) = k) \leq \frac{C}{\sqrt{1+ND_H}} e^{N(F(H)-\beta H k)}
\end{equation}
where $F(H) = \lim_{M} \frac{1}{M} \log \Xi(M,H)$.

