[Lemma lemma_existence_connecting_one_letter_word of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] Consider $w \in \Omega_n^{(0)}$ and $\sigma \in \{-,0,+\}$. For all $h \in \llbracket 1,\#J^{\sigma}-1 \rrbracket$, there exists a one-letter word $\xi^{h,\sigma}=(k)$, with $R \leq |k| \leq R+1$ such that
\begin{equation*}
u^{h,\sigma}\cdot\xi^{h,\sigma} \cdot u^{h+1,\sigma} \in \Omega_{\textup{fin}}.
\end{equation*}

