[Lemma lem:powers-of-P of arXiv:2511.01058, 'Limit profiles and cutoff for the Burnside process on Sylow double cosets'] Let \(P\) be the transition kernel for the Sylow--Burnside process when \(k=1\) and let \(\tilde\psi = \frac{1}{pn_1}\mathbf 1_A-\frac{1}{p^2n_2}\mathbf 1_B\). If \(|H\sigma H|=p\), then
        \begin{align}
            P^t_\sigma & =   \left(1-\frac{1}{p}\right)^t\left(\frac{1}{p}\mathbf 1_{H \sigma H}-\frac{1}{pn_1}\mathbf 1_A\right)            +\frac{n_2}{n_1+n_2}\left(1-\frac{1}{p}-\frac{p-1}{p(p-2)!}\right)^t\tilde\psi+\pi,
        \end{align}
        and if \(|H\sigma H|=p^2\), then
        \begin{equation}
            P^t_\sigma = -\frac{n_1}{n_1+n_2}\left(1-\frac{1}{p}-\frac{p-1}{p(p-2)!}\right)^t\tilde\psi+\pi.
        \end{equation}

