[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] There exists a constant \(C>0\) such that, for all \(n\) sufficiently large,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal E_{A^o}[\mathcal X_n^{\mathrm{geo}},\mathcal X_n^0]
\le
C\frac{\log\log n}{\log n}.
\end{align*}
In particular,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal E_{A^o}[\mathcal X_n^{\mathrm{geo}},\mathcal X_n^0]
\le
C\frac{(\log\log n)^{\mathrm e-\frac32}}{\log n}.
\end{align*}

