[Lemm 4 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] For fixed $h>0$, consider the function $\Phi^{(h)}$ as given by \eqref{eq:Phi}. Then, for any $X \in L^2({\mathbb S})$,  we have
    \begin{align}
	\|\Phi^{(h)}(X)\|_2^2 = \|X\|_2^2  +h.
\end{align}Moreover,  
\begin{align}
\| \Phi^{(h)}(X) - X \|_2^2 \leq h, \\
2 \langle X,\Phi^{(h)}(X)-X \rangle \leq h. 
\end{align}

