[Conj exp_mixing of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] For every $\beta>\beta_c$, there exists $c>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
\begin{equation}
   \sup_{\substack{A\in \sigma(\Lambda_n) \\ B\in \sigma(\Lambda_{2n}^c)}} \big|\Psi_\beta[A\cap B] - \Psi_\beta[A]\Psi_\beta[B]\big| \leq e^{-cn},
\end{equation}
where $\sigma(\Lambda)$ denotes the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $(\omega_e)_{e\in \overline{E}(\Lambda)}$ and $(\mathsf{a}_x)_{x\in\Lambda}$, and where $\Psi_\beta$ denotes the (conjecturally) unique infinite volume measure at parameter $\beta$. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Lemma 43 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] Let $B_0^N$ be a deterministic matrix. There exists a constant $C_{\rho,t}$ such that, for any $y\in\R$, we have that
    \begin{align*}
        &\left| \E\left[\ts_N\left(e^{\i y \left|B^N_0B^N(t)-z\right|^2}\right)\right] - \tau_N\left(e^{\i y |B^N_0b(t)-z|^2}\right) \right| \\
        & \leq C_{\rho,t} \frac{(1+y^4)(1+|z|^4)(1+\norm{B^N_0}^4)}{N^2},
    \end{align*}
    where we used the construction of the space $\A_N$ of Lemma \ref{lem:bigspace} to define the product of $B^N_0$ and $b(t)$.

