 i_2$ of the units is an equivalence again, so that $i_1$ and $i_2$ exhibit $\textbf{\textup{C}}^\otimes\times\textbf{\textup{D}}^\otimes$ as the coproduct, which will then complete the proof of semiadditivity. For this, let us make the tensor product $\textbf{\textup{E}}\times\textbf{\textup{E}}\to\textbf{\textup{E}}$ into a strong symmetric monoidal functor $\mu$ via the associativitiy and symmetry isomorphisms of $\textbf{\textup{E}}^\otimes$, and consider the composite
