[Lemma lem:bounds_for_J_sigma(phi) of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $F \in \mathcal{C}^2$. There exists a random variable $\Psi$ such that for all $s \in [0, 1], x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$, we have 
    \begin{equs}
        \| \blue{F (\phi^{s,x})}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s, 1])}& + \| \blue{J^{s,x}}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s, 1])} + \| \blue{(J^{s,x})^{-1}}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s, 1])}
        \\
        & + \| \blue{\nabla J^{s,x}}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s, 1])} + \|  \blue{\nabla(J^{s,x})^{-1}}\|_{\mathcal{D}^{2H_-}_B([s, 1])}\leq \Psi.
    \end{equs}
    Moreover, for any $p \geq 1$, there exists a constant $C=C( H_-, p, \| \sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^4}, \| F\|_{\mathcal{C}^2})$ such that $\| \Psi \|_{L_p(\Omega)} \leq C$.

