body:
[Lemma lem:block-equi of arXiv:2607.24705, 'Derangetropy Operators'] Let $I \subseteq (0,1)$ be an interval. For almost every $s$, along
		dyadic $N \to \infty$:
		\begin{equation}
			N\,\big\Vert P_{N}u_{s}\big\Vert_{L^{2}(I)}^{2}
			\;\longrightarrow\; \frac{2}{\pi^{2}}\,|I|,
			\qquad
			N\int_{I}\big(\mathrm{Re}\,[e^{i\theta}P_{N}u_{s}]\big)^{2}dz
			\;\longrightarrow\; \frac{1}{\pi^{2}}\,|I|
			\ \text{ uniformly in }\theta,

		\end{equation}
		while the blocks of the density obey the self-referential law
		\begin{equation}
			N\,\big\Vert P_{2N}^{\mathbb{Z}}\,w_{s}\big\Vert_{L^{2}(I)}^{2}
			\;\longrightarrow\; \frac{2}{\pi^{2}}\int_{I}w_{s}(z)\,dz,

		\end{equation}
		where $P_{2N}^{\mathbb{Z}}$ retains the spatial frequencies
		$|k| \in [2N, 4N)$ of $w_{s}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

