[Proposition prop: transport equation with constant threshold of arXiv:2608.23756, 'Measure-valued fluid limits for partial service queues\\with correlated patience and servi'] Fix a constant $y_* \in [0, \infty)$ and let $\bar \boldsymbol{y}_t \vcentcolon= y_*$ for all $t \in [a, b]$. In addition, fix $t \in [a, b]$ and $\phi \in C_c^1(U_g)$, and consider the function defined as:
	\begin{equation*}
		\psi_s^t(x, y) \vcentcolon= \phi\left(x + \int_s^t \mathbbm{1}_{\left\{y + \tau - s \leq y_*\right\}}d\tau, y + t - s\right)
	\end{equation*}
	for all $s \in [a, t]$ and $x, y \in \mathbbm{R}_+$. If $\boldsymbol{\mu} \in \mathcal{S}_{\bar \boldsymbol{y}}[a, b]$ satisfies (equation eq: integrable total variation of the paper), then (equation eq: application of duality method of the paper) holds:
	\begin{equation*}
		L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_t}(\phi) = L_{\boldsymbol{\mu}_a}(\psi_{a}^t) + \lambda_0 \int_{a}^t \psi_s^t(0, 0)ds.
	\end{equation*}

