[Lem LieMon of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] For any word $J=(j_{1},\cdots,j_{m}),$ one has
\begin{equation}
{\rm e}_{[J]}=\sum_{K\subseteq(1,\cdots,m-2)}(-1)^{|K|}{\rm e}_{J\backslash(J_{K},j_{m-1},j_{m})}\otimes[{\rm e}_{j_{m-1}},{\rm e}_{j_{m}}]\otimes{\rm e}_{\overleftarrow{J_{K}}}.
\end{equation}

[Lemma propositionfundamental of arXiv:2608.30443, 'On smooth holosphere solutions to compressible Euler equation'] Pick universal constants $\frac{1}{\delta},\Theta^*\gg 1$, then for all $0<b<b^*(\delta,\Theta^*)\ll1$ small enough, the following holds. Let 
\begin{equation}

\frac{K^{\nu_b+3}\left(b\delta\right)^{K-1}}{\Theta^*}<\alpha_\gamma<1-\frac{K^{\nu_b+3}\left(b\delta\right)^{K-1}}{\Theta^*}
\end{equation}
and  let $u^*(\alpha_\gamma)$ be the solution to (equation neknvonenneudatsgeeaa of the paper) described by Lemma (lemmanekvneneoneon of the paper). Then the $C^\infty$ solution to (equation fineioneoineeogn of the paper) satisfies the bound:
\begin{equation}

\frac{|r_{\mathcal G}|}{M_0}+\frac{|\mathcal T r_{\mathcal G}|}{M_0}<\sqrt{b}.
\end{equation}

