\begin{equation*}
    \mathrm G_{X,Y}'(z) 
    = X \left[-\frac{a}{1+z} + \frac{\ell+a-b-\sqrt{D}}{2} \right] + Y \left[ \frac{b}{z} + \frac{\ell-a+b+\sqrt{D}}{2} \right]. 
\end{equation*}
Noting that $\frac{1}{1+\mathsf{z}_c} = \frac{\ell+a-b-\sqrt{D}}{2a}$ and $\frac{1}{\mathsf{z}_c} = -\frac{\ell-a+b+\sqrt{D}}{2b}$, we see  that $ \mathrm G_{X,Y}'(\mathsf{z}_c) = 0$. 
Also, since
