[Satz theorem:ChaosInIndependentOrPartialLSI of arXiv:2507.08692, 'Some notes on higher order concentration of measure'] Let $\mu$ be a probability measure with support in $[a,b]^n$ for some real numbers $a < b$ which satisfies a $\mathfrak{d}\mathrm{-LSI}(\sigma^2)$. For $f = f(x)$ as in (equation eqn:fTauNew of the paper) and all $r \ge 2$ we have
	\begin{align*}
		\norm{(f - \IE f)_+}_r &\le \sum_{j = 1}^d (2\sigma^2 (b-a)^2 (r-3/2))^{j/2} \IE W_j, \\
		\norm{f - \IE f}_r &\le \sum_{j = 1}^d (2(b-a)^2 r)^{j/2} \IE\tilde{W}_j.
	\end{align*}
	Consequently, for any $t \ge 0$
	\begin{align*}		
			\mu \left( f - \IE f \ge t \right) &\le 2 \exp \Big( - \frac{1}{2\sigma^2(b-a)^2} \min_{j=1,\ldots,d} \Big( \frac{t}{de \IE W_j} \Big)^{2/j} \Big) \\
			&\le 2 \exp \Big( -\frac{1}{2e^2\sigma^2(b-a)^2d^2} \min_{j=1,\ldots,d} \Big( \frac{t}{\IE W_j} \Big)^{2/j}  \Big),
	\end{align*}
	and the same inequalities hold for $\mu(|f-{\mathbb E} f| \ge t)$ with $\IE W_j$ replaced by $\IE \tilde{W}_j$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition semigroup norm bounds of arXiv:2506.21466, 'The Markov property for $\varphi^4_3$ on the cylinder'] There exists $C>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\|\mathbf P_\tau \|_{\mathcal L(\mathcal H)} \leq e^{C \tau }.	
\end{equation}

