[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Assume that (\ref{wlog}) holds. Then, there exists an (random) subset $\Neg_1 \subseteq \Sym_n$ with $\Proba(\pi^* \in \Neg_1) = o(1)$ such that, if $\pi \in \Sym_n \setminus \Neg_1$ and $\sigma$ is an automorphism of $I(\pi)$, 

    \begin{equation}
        \Proba(\sigma\pi | G, H, (p_e)) \geq  \Proba(\pi | G, H, (p_e))e^{-o_\Proba(n \log n)} 
    \end{equation}
    uniformly in $\sigma, \pi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

