[Definition 38 (Sampled vertex sets) of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Fix $h_* \le j \le h^*$.  Conditionally on the tree $\mathscr{T}^n$, we define the sampled vertex set $\widetilde{\cX}_j$ as follows:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If $X_j\ge  \lfloor(\log n)^{1+\frac{\varepsilon}{2}}\rfloor$, let $\widetilde{\cX}_j$ be a uniformly chosen 
        $\lfloor(\log n)^{1+\frac{\varepsilon}{2}}\rfloor$-tuple of $\cX_j$;
        \item Otherwise, let $\widetilde{\cX}_j$ be a uniformly chosen $\lfloor(\log n)^{1+\frac{\varepsilon}{2}}\rfloor$-tuple of $\{x^j_1,\ldots,x^j_{q_n(j)}\}$.
    \end{itemize}
    The choices are (conditionally) independent across heights.

[Theorem 6 (Error bound for the truncated expectation) of arXiv:2604.23133, 'High-Precision Framework for Expected Hitting Times Analysis in the Dice-Sum Process'] Assume there exist finite constants $L_N < U_N$ (depending on $N$ and the geometry of~$\mathcal{H}$) such that 
for all $s \le N$ with $\mathbb{P}_s(A_N) > 0$,
\begin{equation}
L_N < \mathbb{E}_s\!\big[T - \omega_N \,\big|\, A_N\big] < U_N.
\end{equation}
Then,
\begin{equation}
0 < E(s) - \bigl(E_N(s) + L_N\,\mathbb{P}_s(A_N)\bigr)
< (U_N - L_N)\,\mathbb{P}_s(A_N).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma J=0 irredu of arXiv:2511.05223, 'Kac's Program and Relative Entropy Decay for Nonlinear Spin-Exchange Dynamics'] Fix $m\in(-1,1)^\ensuremath{\mathcal A}$, and let \(\pi\) denote the associated product of Bernoulli measures as above with \(m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(\pi)=m\). Then, for every \(\varepsilon > 0\), there exists  \(u := u(\varepsilon, \mathcal{K}, m)\) such that
\begin{equation}
    \|\Phi_u^0(p_1,\dots,p_{2^u}) - \pi\|_{\mathrm{TV}} \le \varepsilon,
\end{equation}
for all choices of \(p_1, \ldots, p_{2^u}\in\ensuremath{\mathcal P}(\O)\) with  \(m_\ensuremath{\mathcal A}(p_i) = m\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem cA7 of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] For any $q\in(0,p)$,
there exists $C\in(0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\sup_{t\in[0, T]}\mathbf{E}^{(N)}_{t_1,\dots,t_N}\Big[\|\Delta_t^n\|^q\Big]
\leq C^{N+1}h_n^{\frac{p-q}{\chi}\wedge q}(1+2\|x\|^{p})+ (2N+1)C^{N+1}
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
for $n$ large enough uniformly over
$N\in\mathbb{N}_0$ and $N$-tuples $\{t_1,\dots, t_N\}\subset (0,T)$.

