[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] There exists $\gamma\in (0,1)$ such that for every $\delta \in (0,1)$ we can find a constant $c_{12}=c_{12}(\delta)>0$ such that for $\bbQ$-a.a.\ $\omega \in \Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}$ there exists $N_0(\omega,\delta) \in \bbN$ such that for every $N \geq N_0(\omega,\delta)$,
    \begin{equation}
        \big|\bbE^{\omega,+}_N[\varphi_x - \varphi_y]\big| \leq  c_{12}\frac{|x-y|_\infty^{\gamma}}{N^{\gamma-\delta}}\,,\qquad \forall x,\,y\in\bbZ^d.
    \end{equation}

