body:
[Proposition eq:lower_semi_continuity of arXiv:2607.18011, 'From local giants to locality in long-range percolation'] \thlabel{prop:lower_semi_continuity}
    Let $G$ be a locally finite transitive graph and let $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ be transitive and integrable.

    Let $(G_n,J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ be a sequence of transitive graphs and kernels converging locally to $(G,J)$ with $(J_n)_{n \in \mathbf{N}}$ uniformly integrable.

    Then

    \begin{equation}

        \liminf_{n \to \infty} 
        \left(
            \beta_c(G_n,J_n)
        \right) 
        \geq 
        \beta_c(G,J). 
    \end{equation}

