body:
[Theorem th1 of arXiv:2412.04973, 'On the Laplace equation with non-local dynamical boundary conditions'] Let $l > 0.$ Then there is an Hilbert basis $\{\varphi_n, n\in  {\mathbb N}\}$ of $L^2(\Gamma)$, $\varphi_n\in \mathcal{D}(\Gamma),$  $\varphi_n$ real valued, and an increasing real sequence $\{\lambda_n,
n\in  {\mathbb N}\}$,   $\lambda_n\to\infty $  as $ n\to\infty,$ each $\lambda_n$ having finite multiplicity, such that for any $n\in {\mathbb N}$ a unique solution  $\psi_n$  (which belongs to $C^\infty(\bar\Omega )$
of the Dirichlet non-homogeneous problem

\begin{align}

\left\lbrace
\begin{array}{ll}
\displaystyle \Delta \psi_n=0 \qquad
&\text{in
$\Omega$,}\\
\psi_n(x)=\varphi_n(x)&\text{on $\Gamma$}
\end{array}
\right.
\end{align}
solves the eigenvalue problem
\begin{align}

\left\lbrace
\begin{array}{ll}
\displaystyle \Delta \psi_n=0 \qquad
&\text{in
$\Omega$,}\\
\lambda_n\psi_n =-k \partial_{\bf n} \psi_n - l \Delta_\Gamma \psi_n \qquad &\text{on
$ \Gamma$.}
\end{array}
\right .
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2608.29406, 'Partially Totally Real Submanifolds of Sasakian Manifolds'] If $F$ is parallel, then
\begin{equation}
 A_{fV}Z=0
\end{equation}
for every $Z\in\Gamma(\Dperp)$ and every normal vector field $V$.

[Theorem 17 (Uniqueness of the Reflection Map) of arXiv:2605.16868, '\ttl'] For a given $X\in\mathcal{D}_T(L_1)$ and $\boldsymbol{F}\in\mathcal{R}$, there exists a unique fixed point $W^*$ of the map $\pi_{X,F}$, that is,
    \begin{equation*}
        W^*_u = (\pi_{X,F}(W^*))_u, \quad \forall\,u\in[0,1].
    \end{equation*}
    Moreover, the regulator map $\Psi_F(X)$ is equal to the fixed point $W^*$, that is,
    \begin{equation*}
        (\Psi_F(X))_u = W^*_u, \quad \forall\,u\in[0,1].
    \end{equation*}

