[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that $\sigma(t,x,y)=\sigma(t,x)$ and Assumptions {\rm\ref{A1}} and {\rm\ref{A2}} hold.
Let $(X_t^\varepsilon,Y_t^\varepsilon)_{t\ge0}$ and $(\bar{X}_t^{\varepsilon})_{t\ge0}$ be the strong solution to the SDEs \eqref{Equation} and \eqref{MAE}, respectively. Then, for any $\varepsilon>0$,  $(x,y)\in\RR^{n}\times\RR^{m}$ and $T>0$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\mathbb{E}|X_{t}^{\varepsilon}-\bar{X}^{\varepsilon}_{t}|^2\le  C_T(1+|x|^2+|y^2|)\varepsilon^{1/3}. 
\end{align}

