body:
[Theorem 31 (Uniform-in-time fixed-marginal chaos in total variation) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:concentration}, together with either kernel assumption, for fixed $k$ and $N\ge2k$,
\begin{equation}
    \sup_{t\ge0}
    \|P_{N,t}^{(k)}-\mu_t^{\otimes k}\|_{\mathrm{TV}}
    \le C_k\left\{
       N^{-\frac{\varepsilon\alpha}{\kappa+2\varepsilon\alpha}}
       +N^{-1/2}\right\},
\end{equation}
where \(C_k\) may depend on \(k\) and the standing model parameters, but is
independent of \(N\) and \(t\).

