[Theorem theorem-cvg-RFIM-partition-function of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$, $a,b \in \partial D$ and $(D_{\delta};a_{\delta},b_{\delta})_{\delta}$ be as in Section (sec_assumptions_domain of the paper). Let $\lambda: \bar D \to (0,\infty)$ be a bounded and continuous function. Let $(H_{x})_{x \in \mathbb{Z}^2}$ be independent Gaussian random variables with mean $0$ and variance $1$ and set, for $x \in D_{\delta}$, $h_x = H_{x/\delta}$. Let $\xi \in \{-,\pm,+\}$.  Then, the rescaled partition function
    \begin{equation} 
        \tilde{\mathcal{Z}}_{\delta}^{\xi,\lambda, h}:= \exp\big(-\frac{\|\lambda\|_{L^{2}}^2}{2}\delta^{-\frac{1}{4}}\big) \mu_{\delta}^{\xi}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\delta^{\frac{7}{8}}\sum_{x \in D_{\delta}}\lambda(x)h_{x}\sigma_{x}\bigg)\bigg]
    \end{equation}
    converges in distribution as $\delta \to 0$ to a random variable $\mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda}$ with Wiener chaos expansion
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda} = 1+ \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{C_{\sigma}^n}{n!}\int_{D^n} f_{D}^{(\xi,n)}(z_1,\dots,z_n) \prod_{j=1}^{n} \lambda(z_j)W(dz_j)
    \end{equation}
    where $W(\cdot)$ denotes white noise on $\mathbb{R}^2$ and where the functions $(f_{D}^{(\xi,n)})_n$ are as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lem: interface exploration probability with number of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $I\subset \Lambda_{M}$ be a subset of $\Lambda_{M}.$ There exists a constant $c_{14}>0$ such that 
for any boundary condition $\eta_I$ on $\mathrm{Ball}(I)$ and any configuration $\xi\in\hat\Sigma_i$, we have
    \begin{align}
	\sum_{\gamma}\mu^{\xi}_{\Lambda_{M}}(\gamma)&\ge c_{14};\\
    \sum_{\gamma}\mu^{\xi,\eta_I}_{\Lambda_{M}\setminus{\mathrm{Ball}(I)}}(\gamma,\tau(\gamma)=k)&\leq (1-c_{14}^{|I|})^{k+1}.
\end{align}

