[Theorem 2 (Absence of positive-time multiple collisions) of arXiv:2605.23529, 'Generalized Bessel-Dunkl diffusions'] Let $x_0\in\Cc$.  Assume \ref{ass:cont}, \ref{ass:sigma}, and \ref{ass:k:positive}.  Then the weak solution $X$ constructed in Theorem~\ref{thm:existence} has no multiple collisions at positive times.  More precisely, for every two different roots $\alpha,\beta \in R_+$ such that $\sum_{i=1}^\no \alpha_i^2\beta_i^2>0$ we have 
        \begin{equation*}
            \inner{X(t)}{\alpha}+\inner{X(t)}{\beta}>0, \qquad 0<t<\life{X}\qquad \textrm{a.s.} 
        \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

