Write $\delta=r_{n,k}-\varepsilon$ and introduce
\begin{equation}
 \mathsf X_\varepsilon=x_\delta,\qquad
 \mathsf Y_\varepsilon=\frac{r_\delta-r_{n,k}}{\varepsilon},\qquad
 \widehat\Theta_\varepsilon=\frac{\theta_\delta}{\varepsilon}.
\end{equation}
The sans-serif letters distinguish the axial and radial perturbation variables
from the immersion $X$ and from the normalised coordinates introduced later;
the hat on $\widehat\Theta_\varepsilon$ distinguishes the scaled angle from
the unscaled tangent angle $\theta_\delta$.
In these variables the exact system is
\begin{equation}
