[Defn restricted of arXiv:2609.01745, 'The Directional Localization Game on Graphs'] Given a tree decomposition $(T, \mathcal{B})$ of width $k$, we call $(T, \mathcal{B})$ a \textit{restricted smooth tree decomposition} of $G$ if:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\Delta(T) \le 3$;
\item $\left \vert B_a \right \vert \in \{k, k+1\}$ for all $a \in V(T)$; and
\item $\left \vert B_a \cap B_b \right \vert = k$ for all $ab \in E(T)$.
\end{itemize}

[Prop 22 (Approximate scaling of the comparison model) of arXiv:2604.23461, 'Scaling limit of Sinkhorn-rescaled Random Matrices \\ via Stability of Static Schrödinger '] Let $(\r, \c)$ be an $m \times n$ positive margin. Under Assumption \ref{assump:random_matrix}, let $(\balpha, \bbeta)$ denote the deterministic Schr\"{o}dinger potentials scaling $\bLambda$ to $(\r, \c)$, and let $\hat{\X}^{\r,\c} = \D(e^{\balpha})\X\D(e^{\bbeta})$ be the comparison model. Define the variance and scale proxies
	\begin{align}
		V_{r} := n\sigma^2 e^{4K}\,\frac{N^2}{\|\bLambda\|_1^2}, \qquad V_{c} := m\sigma^2 e^{4K}\,\frac{N^2}{\|\bLambda\|_1^2}, \qquad B := e^{2K}\,\frac{N R}{\|\bLambda\|_1}.
	\end{align}
	Then, for every $\eps > 0$, $i \in [m]$, and $j \in [n]$,
	\begin{align}
		\P\!\left( \bigl|r_i(\hat{\X}^{\r,\c}) - \r(i)\bigr| \ge \eps\, \r(i) \right) &\le 2\exp\!\left( -\frac{\eps^2 \r(i)^2 / 2}{V_r + B\,\eps\, \r(i)} \right), \\

		\P\!\left( \bigl|c_j(\hat{\X}^{\r,\c}) - \c(j)\bigr| \ge \eps\, \c(j) \right) &\le 2\exp\!\left( -\frac{\eps^2 \c(j)^2 / 2}{V_c + B\,\eps\, \c(j)} \right).
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

