body:
[Lemma lem:Key0 of arXiv:2606.19313, 'Stability of Khintchine-type inequalities via log-monotonicity'] Let $r_k=r_k(X)$ for a random variable $X$. Define $f:\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}^n\to \mathbb{R}$ by setting 
\begin{align*}
f(\alpha_1, \alpha_2, \ldots, \alpha_n)=\prod_ir_{\alpha_i}.
\end{align*}
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $(r_k)$ is log-concave, then $f$ is Schur-concave;\\

\item If $(r_k)$ is log-convex, then $f$ is Schur-convex.
\end{enumerate}

