with $\|N_z^n\|\leq C r^n$ for some $r<1$. On $[-\pi,\pi]^d\setminus(-\delta,\delta)^d$, the aperiodicity condition with $\zeta=0$ gives an exponentially small contribution.

Put $\theta=u/\sqrt n$. The Taylor expansion of $\Lambda(z)=\log\varrho(z)$ gives, uniformly for $u$ in compact ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:a4623c9390855f1b9a9d6fc4af76f10332f1813170522dc3a0521d652ae99dff","revision_digest":"sha256:f6c7254b1e347b58a34c72271a75269f8d0555449f6df1112a55e6370fc539c3","source_id":"arxiv:2607.07283","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

