[Theorem 8 (Resolution invariance) of arXiv:2609.01116, 'Vector-Carleson, Calder\'on, and Poisson--Atomic Criteria for\\ Generalized Hilbert Operat'] Let $2<p<\infty$ and let $\sigma$ be an $(L,M,p)$-admissible analytic
resolution. Then
\[
 \boxed{
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{\sigma}:\ell^p\to H^p\|
 \asymp_{p,L,M}
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}:\ell^p\to H^p\|.}
 \tag{3.10}
\]
For the nonconstant coordinate tails,
\[
\begin{split}
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{\sigma,>N}\|
 &\lesssim_{p,L,M}
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{>N-L}\|,\\
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{>N}\|
 &\lesssim_{p,L}
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{\sigma,>N-L}\|,
\end{split}
 \tag{3.11}
\]
where a negative cutoff means the full nonconstant synthesis.
Consequently,
\[
 \|T_\phi\|_{\mathrm e}
 \asymp_{p,L,M}
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{\sigma,>N}\|,
 \qquad
 T_\phi\text{ is compact}
 \iff
 \|\mathscr S_{\phi,p}^{\sigma,>N}\|\longrightarrow0.
 \tag{3.12}
\]

[Lm of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For any $f, g\in H_0^{1,1}(0,\infty)$, the quadratic form,
    \begin{equation}
        \langle f, \mathcal{H}_{\beta}(t) g\rangle,
    \end{equation}
    is well defined as $\lim_{n \to \infty } \langle f_n, \mathcal{H}_{\beta}(t) g\rangle$ for any $f_n \in C_c^{\infty}(0,\infty)$ with $f_n \to f.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

