[Proposition prop_lower_bound of arXiv:2605.26804, '\Large Large Deviation Principle for the Empirical Measures of Simple Random Walks on $\ov'] For all $\mu \in \mathcal{P}(\overline{\mathbb{Z}})$, 
\begin{equation*}
-I(\mu) \leq \lim_{\varepsilon \to 0^+} \liminf_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \log \mathbb{P}\big( \ell_n \in B(\mu,\varepsilon) \big),
\end{equation*}
where the rate function $I$ is defined in ((eq_def_rate_fuction of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is demicontinuous;
\item[(ii)] The common order and uo adherence of $\Ba_{F}$ is norm bounded;
\item[(iii)] Order adherence preserves norm bounded sets;
\item[(iii')] Uo adherence preserves norm bounded sets. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Recall the definition of $a_n(t)$ from \eqref{E:1.24a}. There exist~$c,\tilde c >0$ such that
\begin{equation}

P^\varrho\Bigl(\,\max_{x\in\BbbL_n}\sqrt{L_t(x)}\ge\sqrt t+a_n(t)+u\Bigr)\le c(1+u)\texte^{-2\slb\, u-\tilde c u^2/n}
\end{equation}
holds for all $n\ge1$,  $t>0$ and all~$u>0$. Moreover, there exist~$c_1,c_2>0$ such that \begin{equation}

P^\varrho\biggl(\,\Bigl|\,\max_{x\in\BbbL_n}\sqrt{L_t(x)}-\sqrt t-a_n(t\vee1)\Bigr|>u\,\bigg|\,\max_{x\in\BbbL_n}L_t(x)>0\biggr)\le c_1\texte^{-c_2 u}
\end{equation}
holds for all~$n\ge1$, all $t>0$ and all $u\in(0,n]$.  Here $s\vee t:=\max\{s,t\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

