[Definition 61 of arXiv:2608.09700, 'A general paracontrolled ansatz for singular SPDEs'] An admissible renormalisation map is a couple $(M,M^+)$ made of a linear maps $M : T \to T$ and an algebra morphism $M^+ : T^+ \to T^+$ such that 
		\begin{equation}
			(M\otimes M^+)\Delta = \Delta M, \qquad \text{and} \qquad (M^+\otimes M^+)\Delta^{\!+} = \Delta^{\!+} M^+,
		\end{equation}
	for any $n\in \N^{d+1}$
		\begin{equation}
			M\mcI_n(\tau) = \mcI_n(M\tau), \qquad \text{and} \qquad 	M^+\mcI^+_n(\tau) = \mcI^+_n (M^+\tau),
		\end{equation}
		and for any $k\in\bfN^{d+1}$
		\begin{equation}
			\downarrow^k M =M\downarrow^k,\qquad \text{and}\qquad \downarrow^k M^{+} =M^{+}\downarrow^k.
		\end{equation}

[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Suppose $X,Y\in \mathcal{H}_1$ and $X$ is independent to $Y$ under the sub-liner expectation $\mbE$. If $\bE[X]=\be[X]=0$ and $\bE[|X|]<\infty, \bE[|Y|]<\infty$, then 
\begin{equation}
    \bE[XY]=0.
\end{equation}

