body:
[Prop proyos of arXiv:2506.08202, 'Stochastic dissipative systems in Banach spaces driven by L\'evy noise'] Assume that Hypotheses (Hyp2 of the paper) or Hypotheses (Hyp1 of the paper)  hold true. For every $x\in E$, there exists a function $y(\cdot,x)\in C([0,T],{H})\cap C_b((0,T],E)$ such that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\delta{\rightarrow} 0}\norm{y_{\delta}(\cdot,x)-y(\cdot,x)}_{C([0,T],{H})}=0,\quad \forall\; T>0,\;
\end{equation}
and $y(\cdot,x)$ is the unique mild solution of (equation eq of the paper). Moreover for every $x,z\in E$ and $t>0$ we have
{\small
\begin{align}
&{\left|y(t,x)\right|}_{H}\leq e^{\zeta t}{\left|x\right|}_{H}+\int_0^te^{\zeta (t-s)}\left({\left|F(f(s))\right|}_{H}+2\max\{0,\zeta_F\}{\left|f(s)\right|}_{H}\right)ds,\\
&{\left\|y(t,x)\right\|}_E\leq e^{\zeta t}{\left\|x\right\|}_E+\int_0^te^{\zeta (t-s)}\left({\left\|F(f(s))\right\|}_E+2\max\{0,\zeta_F\}{\left\|f(s)\right\|}_E\right)ds,	\\
&{\left|y(t,x)-y(t,z)\right|}_{H}\leq  e^{\zeta t}{\left|x-z\right|}_{H}\\
&{\left\|y(t,x)-y(t,z)\right\|}_E\leq  e^{\zeta t}{\left\|x-z\right\|}_E,
\end{align}
}
where $\zeta$ is the constant defined in (equation zeta of the paper). In addition if Hypotheses (Hyp2 of the paper) holds true then for every $x\in E$
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\theta{\rightarrow} 0}\norm{y_{\delta}(\cdot,x)-y(\cdot,x)}_{C([\epsilon,T],E)}=0,\quad \forall\;\epsilon>0,
\end{equation}

