[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. For $z\in\C^+$ with $|z-E_*|<\eps_*$,
        \begin{align}
                \left\|\Pi(z)-\Pi_* -\Theta(z)\Pi_*\calE[\f{r}_*]\Pi_*\right\| \lesssim |\Theta(z)|^2. 
        \end{align}
        With respect to the basis $\{\f{r}_*,\wh{\f{r}}_*\}$ and its dual basis $\{\f{\ell}_*,\wh{\f{\ell}}_*\}$, the matrix representation of $\calI-\calJ(z)$ is
        \begin{align}
                \begin{pmatrix} -2\mu_2\Theta(z)+O(|\Theta(z)|^2) & O(|\Theta(z)|)         \\
                O(|\Theta(z)|)                    & 1-\la_*+O(|\Theta(z)|)\end{pmatrix}. 
        \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

