[Lemma lem:limit-u' of arXiv:2604.20094, 'Persistence and local extinction for superprocesses in random environments'] Let $f\in C_c^+({\mathbb R}^d)$, and $\nu\in{\mathcal M}_F({\mathbb R}^d)$. Then for each $t\geqslant 0$ and $\lambda\geqslant 0$,
  	\begin{equation}
  		\lim_{\delta\to 0}{\mathbf E} \int_{{\mathbb R}^d}|w_\delta(\lambda; t,x)-  \partial_\lambda u (\lambda; t,x)|\nu(\mathrm{d} x)=0,
    \end{equation}
  	and
  	\begin{equation}
  		\lim_{\delta\rightarrow 0}{\mathbf E} \int|v(t,x)-  \partial_\lambda u (\delta; t,x)|^2\nu(\mathrm{d} x)= 0.
  	\end{equation}

[Lemma lem:gaus_comp_can of arXiv:2607.04514, 'Boundary-layer asymptotics for Gaussian-smoothed singular measures'] Assume (ass:standing of the paper)~(ass:standing:chart of the paper). Fix \(A>0\). There are constants \(c_0,C>0\) such that
  \begin{equation*}
    e^{-\Psi(\zeta;a,x)} \leqslant C\Gamma_{c_0}(\zeta;a), \quad \text{for all}
    \quad x\in\mathcal{K}_{\mathcal{S}},\, \|a\|\leqslant A,\, \zeta\in\mathbb H_c^m.
  \end{equation*}
  Consequently, for every \(R\in(0,\infty]\), every \(\sigma_0>0\), every \(0\leqslant s\leqslant
  r\) and every \(P\in\mathfrak P_s\) on \(\mathcal D_{R,A,\mathcal{K}_{\mathcal{S}},\sigma_0} \), one has
  \(e^{-\Psi}P \in \mathfrak G_s\) on the same domain.

