[Proposition thm|BoundAijPl of arXiv:2504.08938, 'Fourier Levels and Almost Sure Bounds on Higher-Order Derivatives in First-Passage Percola'] Assume that $a/(b-a)\in\mathbb N$.
Let $\zeta>0$. There is a constant $C$ that depends only on $\zeta$, $a$, $b$, and $p$ such that 
\begin{eqnarray}
\sum_{i,j}\left(\mathbb P(A_{\{i,j\}}^+)\right)^{1+\zeta}&\leq&C\cdot n^{2+\zeta-\zeta d}.

\end{eqnarray}

