Let $\xi_i\in L^2(\mathcal{F}_T)$, $i=1,2$ and denote by $(Y^i,Z^i)$ the solution of the mean field BSDE \eqref{MFBSDE'} with parameters $(\xi_i,f_i)$, $i=1,2$. Then, if $\xi_1\leq \xi_2$ and $f_1(t,\mu,y,z)\leq f_2(t,\mu,y,z)$ for all $(\mu,y,z)$, we have $Y^1_t\leq Y^2_t$, $t\in[0,T]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

