Multiplying both sides of equation ((eqn:Y of the paper)) with $ Y_\lambda(t) \cdot | Y_\lambda(t)\vert^{p-2} $ , $p>2$ and then integrating over $\mathbb{T}^2$; we get
\begin{align}
    \frac{1}{p}\partial_t\| Y_\lambda\Vert_{p}^{p}+ \gamma \| Y_\lambda(t)\Vert_{p}^{p}&= -\langle u(t)\cdot \nabla Y_\lambda(t)+ u(t)\cdot \nabla Z_\lambda(t), Y_\lambda(t) \cdot | Y_\lambda(t)\vert^{p-2}\rangle \nonumber \\&\ \  + \langle  (\lambda-\gamma)  Z_\lambda(t), Y_\lambda(t) \cdot | Y_\lambda(t)\vert^{p-2}  \rangle.
    \end{align}
