[Prop 10 of arXiv:2605.25762, 'Brownian Convergence of Planar Domains and Stability of the Planar Skorokhod Embedding Pro'] Let $p>0$. If for some $0<\delta<\tfrac{1}{2}$,
\begin{equation}
\max\left(\int^{\delta}_{0}|q_{n}-q|^{p}\,du,\int^{1}_{1-\delta}|q_{n}-q|^{p}\,du\right)\underset{n\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}0,
\end{equation}
then $\varphi_{n}\underset{n\to\infty}{\longrightarrow}\varphi$ in
$L^{p}_{2\pi}$ .

[Lemma lemma4.7 of arXiv:2609.02607, 'Spatial inhomogeneity for a three-dimensional doubly degenerate nutrient system with indir'] Let $K > 0$ be such that (equation 1.6 of the paper) holds and suppose $u_0\not\equiv$ const.. Then there exists $\delta_2=\delta_2(K,u_0)>0$ such that if $(u_0,v_0,w_0)$ satisfy (equation 1.2 of the paper) and (equation 1.6 of the paper), as well as
\begin{align*}
    \int_{\Omega}v_0< \delta_2,
\end{align*}
the corresponding limit function $u_{\infty}\in C(\Omega)$ from Lemma (lemma4.5* of the paper) satisfies

$u_{\infty} \not\equiv$ const..

