[Cor 37 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma \in [1, \; 3/2)$ and fix $\lambda$ such that $0 < \lambda < 3-2 \gamma$. For every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, let $L_n:=n^{1 - \lambda}$. There exists some $f: \mathbb{N}_+ \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} f(n)=0$, such that for any $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$,
	\begin{align*}
	\forall n \in \mathbb{N}_+, \quad	\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{  \frac{\Theta(n) K_n}{n \sqrt{n} } \sum_{z=1}^{L_n-1}  za(z) \int_s^t \dd r \sum_{x}   \nabla H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor x - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )   \Psi_{x,L_n}^{\alpha,\beta}(\eta_r^n)  \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq \widehat{C} (t-s)^{2} f(n). 
	\end{align*}

