body:
[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Fix \(H\in(\frac{1}{2},1)\) and \(\beta<H\). Assume that \(G,H\) are Lipschitz continuous and globally bounded, \(F \) is $\gamma$-H\"older continuous \(\gamma<1\) such that \(\gamma+\beta>1\). Then, there exists a unique weak solution to the following Young-It\^o SDE
\begin{equation}
\dd Z_t = G_tZ_t \dd t+F_t Z_t \dd B^H_t + H_t\dd \hat W_t,\ \bar Z_0 = z,
\end{equation}
where the first integral is defined in the Young sense and the last one is in the It\^o sense. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

